loom untracked_probe=scan_before:0 scan_after:1 repointer_before:nothing_to_do repointer_after:repointed
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Bakery block: the recovery, the nine links landing, the renumber, and the repointer's untracked blindness claimed for the next lap
file construction/REDS.md the headline re-derived to 621 rows by the monotone witness rather than typed
file construction/archive/REDS-an-enumeration-standing-for-a-rule-rows-621.md the recovered row, renumbered from `%619` with the erratum naming why
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md the peer's `%617` line kept, the recovered row's fold line added at its own stamp
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri `dayshelf_merge` declared `tier lap` with its measured cost, closing the undeclared ratchet
file tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_scan.sh the recovered third correction arm, with the rule written above the case that spells it
file tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_control.sh the recovered six phases, 66 behaviors over 23 pens
file tools/f/fold_shelf_link_witness.rish the recovered seven asserts and the header moved from two corrections to three
obs ERRATUM `20260908.090250`, written after the send because the send is what produced it. The row landed at `%624`, not the `%621` the think lines above name. The first rebase found three more peer rows published while this commit was being written -- `%621`, `%622`, `%623` -- so the same renumber ran a second time in one lap. It cost one line again, for the same reason: every citation of the row spells the stamp `20260908.072125`. The `derived-spine` allocator refused to answer `--next` mid-rebase, which is correct and which I had not met before: a tree with an in-flight row counts it as taken, so the number is read after the rebase rather than during it.
obs AND THE HOT PASS EARNED ITS KEEP ON MY OWN PROSE. Two guards the cold pass had skipped as unmoved reddened on the card block I wrote this lap: `unshared_citation` refused `%621` on a living surface because the anointed spine had bound only to `%620` -- rule 4 of `derived-spine` doing exactly its job on the exact number that was about to move again -- and `vocabulary_collection` refused the word `corpus` in reader prose where the tree's own scans already say population. Both repaired and green by name before the commit.
scope one recovery -- a finished Bakery lap lifted out of a round-open stash, plus one ratchet red
status GREEN -- fold_shelf_link, fold_shelf_link_repoint, reds_ledger_monotone and standing_equipment_scan all green on metal here after the recovery; card graded A+, roster B+
recommend keep-going -- the repointer's corpus is the next lap in this lane: the gate keeps `git ls-files`, the repair reads the working tree, and the control's two untracked legs invert
